ZVSE2
; WoG Debug - battle triggers: counts !?BR, !?BG0, !?BG1 and !?MF1 and remembers what they saw, so the command bridge
; can check them ("vars i wogdebug_br wogdebug_round wogdebug_bg0 wogdebug_bg1 wogdebug_action wogdebug_stack
; wogdebug_side wogdebug_target wogdebug_mf wogdebug_damage wogdebug_hit"). Loaded only while WoG Debug is on.

!?BR;
!!VRi^wogdebug_br^:+1;
!!VRi^wogdebug_round^:Sv997;

!?BG0;
!!VRi^wogdebug_bg0^:+1;
!!BG:A?i^wogdebug_action^ N?i^wogdebug_stack^ Q?i^wogdebug_side^ E?i^wogdebug_target^;

!?BG1;
!!VRi^wogdebug_bg1^:+1;

!?MF1;
!!VRi^wogdebug_mf^:+1;
!!MF:D?i^wogdebug_damage^ N?i^wogdebug_hit^;
